{
 "_about": "Every specimen of the --format-fixes family in one collection, each carrying its own expectation: the calls the fixes must deliver with the flag on (an empty list: none), whether the flag-off run raises the fail-loud hint, and whether the fixes change anything at all (a normal-path call is the same with them off).  serve/test_server.py's FormatFixCorpus runs all of them (plus the four live failures of #804, from stranded_tool_call_failures.json) at three chunk sizes with stream_tools on and off, and asserts nothing that already streamed differs with the fixes on.  A new shape is a data append here, not new test code - and a change to any trigger re-runs the whole recorded world, so fixing one case cannot silently break another.  'class' is the shape's kind (act / mention / envelope / cut / known-miss / same); 'source' is where it was seen; class known-miss documents a real shape no fix covers today.",
